From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:32:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] secur32: Implement the CredSSP security package.

Wine has never had one, and Microsoft's Remote Desktop client authenticates
through it.

The package is the whole MS-CSSP exchange: its own TLS session through
Schannel, SPNEGO/NTLM tokens carried inside DER-encoded TSRequests, the
public key of the TLS session signed with the authentication context to bind
the two together, and the credentials delegated at the end.

Two things worth knowing before changing it. The last authentication token
must travel with the public key: MS-CSSP has the client send both in one
TSRequest, and a server whose own authentication has nothing further to say
reads the public key out of the request that completed the authentication
rather than waiting for another message. And Wine's NTLM is a front end for
Samba's ntlm_auth, so without winbind installed
AcquireCredentialsHandle(L"NTLM") fails before any token is produced.

Signed-off-by: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit cfd62d267cc25671365955af92f9841e9dc13de0)

diff --git a/dlls/secur32/Makefile.in b/dlls/secur32/Makefile.in
index 5f1c58b9b2c..1cf2b623cdb 100644
--- a/dlls/secur32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/secur32/Makefile.in
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ DELAYIMPORTS = crypt32 ncrypt rpcrt4
 UNIX_CFLAGS  = $(GNUTLS_CFLAGS)
 
 SOURCES = \
+	credssp.c \
 	lsa.c \
 	lsass.idl \
 	negotiate.c \
diff --git a/dlls/secur32/credssp.c b/dlls/secur32/credssp.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..38706d6cbb9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/secur32/credssp.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1217 @@
